fafd4a8ab13a9d1118e251e9-question-0\", \"changed_fields\": [\"experiment_id\", \"executions\", \"conclusion\", \"defect_claim\", \"rationale\", \"knowledge\", \"counterevidence\", \"limitations\"]}]}\n07:29:24\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"submission\":\"update.json\",\"summary\":\"The last experiment ran, and its receipt qualifies my own source-only reading in the honest direction. In the slow trial the FSM slept 25ms inside every Apply, all 400 fired applies were eventually accepted, the backlog at the probe was a single entry, and VerifyLeader — answered inside the main loop for a single voter — took 6ms against an idle baseline of 0ms; in the control, with the same flood and no sleeping FSM, the backlog was zero and the probe took 0ms. Both declared comparisons held and are complete, so the leak is real and bounded: the main loop waits about one FSM apply per batch it delivers, and the lag does not accumulate, because the pipeline throttles the client's own Apply calls instead of building a queue. The stronger phrasing I had recorded a few turns ago — that non-progress lasts as long as the FSM lags behind its commits — is therefore narrowed by measurement, and the suspicion that a slow FSM stalls the leader materially is refuted for this configuration, with the residual named plainly: the throttle is the client's call path, so a deployment using BatchApplyCh, which buffers that path, is the configuration where a queue could accumulate and which this run did not exercise. That closes the run with its record internally consistent. Standing in it: three execution-grounded findings with retained receipts, declared comparisons, witnesses and scoped limits — the startup replay that blocks NewRaft once the committed-but-unapplied window exceeds the FSM channel's batch capacity, with the constructor's blocked stack in the retained run; the nonvoter acknowledgement that satisfies VerifyLeader's voter quorum, sustained over twenty mixed-timer trials and coinciding with committed state the confirming leader never applied, bounded for uniform clusters down to a one-millisecond margin with the separating gate identified; and the membership change that installs a voter immediately against two published descriptions that promise staging — alongside five suspicions refuted by evidence rather than argument, one behaviour entry corrected under its own id, every registered question answered, and no necessary gap outstanding. Nothing in it required weakening a requirement or suppressing contrary evidence; several of my own earlier readings were narrowed or refuted by their own receipts, and those narrowings are retained.\"}"}}
